  "summary": "Four candidate documents directly apply Bayesian hierarchical models (multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling) to sepsis (early prediction of septic deterioration). [V0017] (El-Sayed et al., 2022) evaluates this method on the Atlas-ICU dataset, reporting AUROC of 0.69. [V0019] (Gupta et al., 2024) applies the same method to the LedgerGuard dataset, achieving accuracy of 0.83. [V0018] (Fischer et al., 2023) reports F1 of 0.76 on the AgriSat-4 dataset. [V0020] (Haddad et al., 2025) applies the method to CellLife, reporting MAE of 0.90. A fifth document that is closely related but uses a different method is [V0005] (Brennan et al., 2019), which applies self-attention encoder models to sepsis prediction on Atlas-ICU with F1 of 0.71; it is included as the next-best sepsis-prediction study when only four direct Bayesian hierarchical model applications are available. Documents mentioning sepsis prediction only as prior work (e.g., [V0177], [V0111], [V0088], [V0193]) are excluded as non-applications.",
